From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:05:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: accept pipeline-statistics query pools, with every
 counter 0

Red Dead Redemption 2's Vulkan renderer creates a pipeline-statistics
query pool (8 queries, all 11 counters), begins and ends its queries and
copies their results, without enabling pipelineStatisticsQuery, which
KosmicKrisp does not report: Metal has no statistics counters on Apple
GPUs. That is invalid usage, but other drivers tolerate it, and
KosmicKrisp reached UNREACHABLE in kk_reports_per_query when the pool was
created.

Give such a pool one report per enabled counter, as a transform
feedback pool has two, and record nothing between begin and end: the
reports keep the zeros of the last reset, and the end makes the query
available as it does for the other types. Host results and
vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults then go through the existing paths: one zero
per counter, the availability where asked, in 32 or 64 bits.
pipelineStatisticsQuery stays unreported, so an application that checks
it still knows the counts are not real.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-17-rdr2-vulkan-needs.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
index 6039fda..4e36bcc 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@ kk_reports_per_query(struct kk_query_pool *pool)
    case VK_QUERY_TYPE_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_STREAM_EXT:
       /* Primitives written, primitives needed */
       return 2;
+   case VK_QUERY_TYPE_PIPELINE_STATISTICS:
+      /* One per counter. Metal has no statistics counters and the device
+       * reports no pipelineStatisticsQuery; a pool is accepted for
+       * applications that create one anyway, and every counter stays 0. */
+      return util_bitcount(pool->vk.pipeline_statistics);
    default:
       UNREACHABLE("Unsupported query type");
    }
@@ -72,6 +77,12 @@ kk_pool_is_ts(struct kk_query_pool *pool)
    return pool->vk.query_type == VK_QUERY_TYPE_TIMESTAMP;
 }
 
+static inline bool
+kk_pool_is_ps(struct kk_query_pool *pool)
+{
+   return pool->vk.query_type == VK_QUERY_TYPE_PIPELINE_STATISTICS;
+}
+
 /* Only occlusion queries remap their index, into the device's visibility
  * buffer; every other pool keeps its reports in its own BO. */
 static uint64_t
@@ -460,6 +471,11 @@ kk_CmdBeginQueryIndexedEXT(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer, VkQueryPool queryPool,
       return;
    }
 
+   /* Pipeline statistics count nothing: the reports keep the zeros of the
+    * last reset, and the end makes them available. */
+   if (kk_pool_is_ps(pool))
+      return;
+
    cmd->state.gfx.occlusion.mode = flags & VK_QUERY_CONTROL_PRECISE_BIT
                                       ? MTL_VISIBILITY_RESULT_MODE_COUNTING
                                       : MTL_VISIBILITY_RESULT_MODE_BOOLEAN;
@@ -478,7 +494,7 @@ kk_CmdEndQueryIndexedEXT(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer, VkQueryPool queryPool,
    if (pool->vk.query_type == VK_QUERY_TYPE_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_STREAM_EXT) {
       assert(index < ARRAY_SIZE(cmd->state.gfx.xfb.query));
       cmd->state.gfx.xfb.query[index] = 0u;
-   } else {
+   } else if (!kk_pool_is_ps(pool)) {
       cmd->state.gfx.occlusion.mode = MTL_VISIBILITY_RESULT_MODE_DISABLED;
       cmd->state.gfx.dirty |= KK_DIRTY_OCCLUSION;
    }
